# Revalidate by Webhook

Instead of time‑based, you can trigger revalidation from an API route when data changes.

```js
// pages/api/revalidate.js
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  await res.revalidate('/posts');
  return res.json({ revalidated: true });
}
```

Call this endpoint from your CMS webhook, database trigger, or after a Server Action.

You can also revalidate by **tag**: `revalidateTag('posts')`.

